Core Prompt TypesInstruction Prompts: Direct commands that tell the AI exactly what to do using action verbs (e.g., "Write an executive summary of this memo").Role-Based (Persona) Prompts: Asks the AI to assume a specific identity, profession, or viewpoint (e.g., "Act as a financial analyst reviewing this report").Contextual Prompts: Provides essential background information, formatting guidelines, or target audience details to frame the request accurately.Question Prompts: Traditional queries framed as questions, primarily used to request explanations, brainstorm ideas, or conduct research.Advanced Prompting TechniquesZero-Shot Prompting: Asking the AI to perform a task with no examples provided, relying entirely on its foundational training.Few-Shot Prompting: Giving the AI one or more examples of a desired input/output pairing before assigning the actual task, allowing the model to mimic the exact tone and structure.Chain-of-Thought (CoT) Prompting: Instructing the model to "think step-by-step" or outline its reasoning process before delivering a final answer.
